[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) holds **412 unique reports** (the export has 427 rows; 15 ids
repeat). They are not one bug. They are two problems with two different fixes. Counts are
the desk's own view (its cause table, below).

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued fix covers only the first problem. It does not fix the second.
</Callout>

## The two problems

| Problem | Reports | Ticket |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **parser**: the shared parser reads every date month first, so day-first tenants get flipped dates | 379 | [#7](https://github.com/skligerman/mega/issues/7) |
| **hint**: the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY`. Day-first people type it, and the form reads it their way | 33 | [#8](https://github.com/skligerman/mega/issues/8) |

379 + 33 = 412 unique reports. Each report is in one ticket.

## How it ended

The desk closed #4471 on 5 October.

| Problem | Outcome | Ticket |
| --- | --- | --- |
| parser | **Fixed**: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` | #7, closed |
| hint | **Won't fix**: the booking-v3 form is retired | #8, closed |

## What the desk's table shows

The table below is computed from the export. It splits by tenant and channel, so it shows
**379 parser** and **33 hint**. It files 5 one-day reports under parser and footnotes them.
They stay in the parser count.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## How to tell them apart

- **Do not use intake's tag.** It comes from the reporter's browser. It tags 42 reports as
  `hint`. Only 33 are.
- **Use the tenant and the channel.** Day-first tenant, form channel, booking-v3 form: hint.
  Day-first tenant, any other way in: parser.

## What we are not sure of

Five parser reports (R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, R-41620) are one day off, not day and
month swapped. One mentions a client in Lisbon who got Tuesday while a client in Toronto got
Monday. That may be a time-zone effect. We did not give it its own ticket: the desk files them
under parser, and the cause is not proven. Check them again after the parser fix.

## Lessons

- Merging by subject line puts different bugs in one ticket. Read the body before you merge.
- Say which count you use. The desk counts by tenant and channel.

